 **Parameters:**
-*   **Isovalue:** The scalar threshold for extraction.
-*   **Grid Resolution:** $N_x, N_y, N_z$ [S1, unofficial].
+*   `isovalue`: The threshold scalar value. Typical values depend on the data range (e.g., 0.5 for normalized occupancy).
+*   `lower`, `upper`: Bounds for the scalar field. Not given in the sources.
 
 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Voids:** The standard MC algorithm (15 configurations) can generate voids. This is handled by increasing configurations to 24 [S4, abstract only, unofficial].
-*   **Face-Saddle Ambiguities:** The trilinear interpolant has face-saddle ambiguities that require resolution (e.g., via Asymptotic Decider) [S3].
-*   **Thread Synchronization:** Multi-threading requires careful synchronization using critical regions to avoid race conditions when writing to shared output structures [S4, abstract only, unofficial].
+*   **Degenerate Triangles:** Standard Marching Cubes can produce degenerate triangles in specific configurations. Marching Cubes 2 may mitigate this via its lookup table, but this is not guaranteed unless using the "Extended Marching Cubes with No Degenerate Triangles" variant [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Topology Errors:** Like standard Marching Cubes, MC2 may suffer from topological ambiguities in cases 6 and 7 if the lookup table does not account for the trilinear interpolant [S1, unofficial]. For topological correctness, [Marching Cubes 33](5986-marching-cubes-33.md) or [Marching Cubes with Topological Correction](4349-marching-cubes-with-topological-correction-case-6c.md) should be considered.
+*   **Discontinuous Data:** If the input is a Discrete Indicator Function (DIF), standard linear interpolation (used in MC2) causes aliasing. Use [Contouring Discrete Indicator Functions](4087-contouring-discrete-indicator-functions.md) instead [S1, unofficial].
 
